joint_controller -- licences and provenance
===========================================

joint_controller is real-world-rl code, distributed under the MIT License below. The joint
impedance law, its velocity filter and the default gains are ported from the public GELLO
controller (Apache License 2.0), and the joint limit tables are franka_description's
(Apache License 2.0); those parts stay under the Apache License 2.0 (section 2). The package as a
whole is therefore "MIT AND Apache-2.0".

1. real-world-rl's own code (MIT)
---------------------------------
  include/joint_controller/planner.hpp, src/planner.cpp
      the online quintic reference generator (duration selection, exact extrema, bounded stop),
      derived from the standard quintic boundary-value problem;
  include/joint_controller/{law,motion,params}.hpp, src/{law,motion,params}.cpp,
  python/bindings.cpp, python/joint_controller/
      the law around the ported impedance term (reference, timeout stop, coriolis, torque-rate
      limit), the parameter table and validation, the franky torque motion and its mailboxes,
      the Python binding;
  tests/, tools/, docker/, scripts/.

